# Logistics Data Analyst Internship — Week 1

**Task:** Strategic Planning and Data Exploration in Logistics

This repository accompanies the Week 1 strategic planning report submitted for
the Logistics Data Analyst Internship. It contains the illustrative Python
pipeline referenced in Section 8 of the report (data cleaning, exploratory
analysis, a delivery-time regression model, and route clustering).

## Scenario
A mid-size e-commerce retailer operating three regional warehouses is
experiencing rising transportation costs, late deliveries during peak
weekday afternoons, and inconsistent stock availability. This project uses
historical order, inventory, and delivery data to diagnose the causes and
recommend data-driven improvements.

## Files
- `analysis_pipeline.py` — data cleaning, EDA, regression model, and clustering
- `requirements.txt` — Python dependencies
- `Week1_Logistics_Strategic_Planning_Report.docx` — full written report

## How to run
```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
python analysis_pipeline.py
```
(Expects `orders.csv` and `deliveries.csv` with order/delivery fields such as
`order_id`, `warehouse_id`, `destination_zip`, `delivery_time_hrs`,
`promised_time_hrs`, `day_of_week`, `distance_km`, `order_volume`.)

## Status
Week 1 deliverable — planning and pseudocode stage. Weeks 2–4 will apply this
